request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The request asks to remove todos whose "completed" field is true. The Todo type marks completion with `done` (the existing `complete` command sets it), so I'm treating "completed" as `done === true`. To add the command, types needs a new Command variant, and commands needs a clear() function plus handling in parseArgs and run.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 17/17 tests pass). The manifest now shows clear(todos) exported from commands and { kind: "clear" } in the Command union. The request said "completed", but the Todo type only has `done`, so clear removes todos where done === true. parseArgs and run handle the new command.)

